mean_label_low_budget / mean_label_high_budget).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Single-run self-diagnostic (frozen selected configuration)\",\n      \"role\": \"proposed\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"The studied method: from one run's coalition masks, weights and values it simulates reruns via a delete-one-group jackknife (4 partitions, antithetic common-random-number draws), shrinks toward a budget-dependent prior and adds a small margin gate, outputting r_hat in [0,1]. Constants are hand-set and untuned; say so.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Evaluator-owned reference baselines\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Always-reliable (r=1), constant 0.5, and a split-half-gap heuristic computed from the same single run. Grounded via final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable, skill_vs_constant_half, skill_vs_gap_heuristic and their CI lows. The original search-time baseline program has no grounded score in paper_data, so that comparison is omitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Label-permuted pairing control\",\n      \"role\": \"ablation\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Shuffles which r_hat is paired with which instance label (20 deterministic derangements) to separate budget/cell-level calibration from instance-specific information. Score 0.9701 vs diagnostic 0.9838 (final.metric.control_permuted_score, combined_minus_control_ci_low). The key calibration guard of the paper.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Search-plane model variants (three configurations)\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Supplement-only: three scored configurations on search datasets (result.improvement_001..003) show the selection and that differences are small; no component ablations exist, so no mechanistic attribution is claimed. All 3 attempts were scored; there are no unscored attempts.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_focus\": [\n    \"Conditional reliability: final mean label 0.8065 at 4d vs 0.9315 at 16d budget (final.metric.mean_label_low_budget, mean_label_high_budget); single-run top-3 set reproducibility is not uniformly high, and the low-budget regime is where one run is least trustworthy. Do not break this down by dataset or model family; no grounded breakdown exists.\",\n    \"Diagnostic accuracy on final data: combined score 0.9838 (= 1 - mean squared error, so MSE about 0.0162; derived arithmetic, label it derived) with seed-level scores 0.9850 and 0.9826 (final.evidence.episodes, seeds 9001/9002).\",\n    \"Skill over baselines with one-sided 2.5th-percentile bootstrap lower bounds: vs always-reliable +0.0353 (low 0.0171), vs constant 0.5 +0.1543 (low 0.1245), vs split-half gap heuristic +0.0122 (low 0.0081). Only lower bounds are available; do not fabricate upper bounds or symmetric intervals.\",\n    \"Honest control: permuted-pairing score 0.9701; diagnostic minus control = 0.0137 (derived), lower bound 0.0101. Interpret as real but small instance-specific information on top of budget-level calibration; Spearman between r_hat and label 0.581 indicates moderate ranking ability.\",\n    \"Scale of the gain in plain terms: root-mean-squared error about 0.127 for the diagnostic vs about 0.227 for always-reliable (both derived from grounded metrics; label as derived).\",\n    \"Selection is reported separately from the final evaluation: search scores 0.9760, 0.9837, 0.9854 for three scored configurations on the search datasets; the frozen selected configuration is the 0.9854 one. Per-attempt two-seed ranges overlap, so the ordering is not claimed significant.\",\n    \"Final outcome is qualified (final.qualification.outcome); no failed-qualification disclosure needed, but qualification does not turn these bounded metrics into general validity claims.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_plan\": [\n    \"Fig. 1 (overview, early): the measurement protocol and claim structure at a glance: trained model + instance -> one assessed Kernel SHAP run at budget 4d or 16d -> diagnostic outputs r_hat; evaluator reruns 8 times -> top-3 Jaccard label; scoring against always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap, permuted control.\",\n    \"Fig. 2 (main evidence, two panels): (a) skill (MSE reduction) over always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap heuristic, and over permuted control, with one-sided bootstrap lower-bound markers; (b) mean single-run top-3 agreement at 4d vs 16d budget.\",\n    \"Table 1 (native LaTeX): final metrics with lower bounds, seed-level scores and the derived MSE/RMSE column marked as derived.\",\n    \"Supplement Fig./Table: search-plane scores of the three configurations with per-seed values (supporting only).\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_specs\": [\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"protocol_overview\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Give glance value for the setting: what a single run is, what the label measures (top-3 Jaccard vs 8 reruns), what the diagnostic sees, and what it is scored against.\",\n@misc{Lundberg2017Unified\n@misc{Yuan2022empirical\n@misc{Musco2024Provably\n@misc{Chen2020True\n@misc{Marx2019Predictive\n@misc{Ding2021Retiring\n@misc{Gorishniy2021Revisiting\n@misc{Lundberg2018Consistent\n@misc{AlvarezMelis2018Robustness\n@misc{Sundararajan2019many\n@misc{Kumar2020Problems\n@misc{Jethani2021FastSHAP\n@misc{Covert2020Explaining\n@misc{Gosiewska2019Do\n@misc{Mitchell2021Sampling\n@misc{Ribeiro2016Why\n@article{Pedregosa2012Scikit\n@misc{DoshiVelez2017Towards\n@misc{Frye2020Shapley\n@misc{Grinsztajn2022tree\n@misc{Williamson2020Efficient","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
